\cf0 Either way, I can tell you what the 
\f1\b fundamental root cause
\f0\b0  is that keeps defeating every fix:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 overflow: hidden creates a scroll container.
\f0\b0  Even though you can't actually scroll it, Chromium's caret-visibility algorithm walks up the DOM, finds that scroll container, tries to use it to scroll the caret into view, fails because nothing can actually scroll, and the caret renders in the wrong coordinate space. This is why the caret floats up into the middle of the list instead of sitting at the bottom where you're typing.\
The real fix is overflow: clip \'97 it clips content without creating a scroll container, so Chromium's caret algorithm never gets confused.\
Test that and let me know. This is the fix that most AI tools miss because overflow: clip is less well-known than overflow: hidden \'97 they look identical visually but behave completely differently for Chromium's caret-tracking system.\
