\cf0 Let me look at the CSS for the time card textarea/backdrop to understand the layout before touching anything.\
Now I see the exact problem. There are two CSS issues and one JS issue causing what you're describing:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Bug 1 (cursor moves up when scrolling at bottom):
\f0\b0  .time-card-notes-shell uses overflow: hidden \'97 same overflow: hidden 
\f6 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  false scroll container problem. The browser's caret algorithm tries to scroll it and the caret drifts.\

\f1\b Bug 2 (cursor jumps on Enter):
\f0\b0  renderBackdrop calls syncBackdropScroll() synchronously right after innerHTML is replaced \'97 at that moment backdrop.scrollHeight is still the OLD value. So the sync sets the wrong position, then the rAF corrects it a frame later. That's the visible jump.\

\f1\b Bug 3 (drift accumulates over many lines):
\f0\b0  .time-card-app__notes-prefix--time-range is display: inline-block with default vertical-align: baseline. This causes the inline-block's baseline to shift the line box height slightly in the backdrop but not in the transparent textarea, making their scrollHeight diverge over many lines.\
All three fixes:\
Now remove the synchronous syncBackdropScroll() from renderBackdrop \'97 the scroll listener handles live sync, the rAF handles post-layout sync. The synchronous call with stale heights is what causes the jump:\
